From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 13:34:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(memory): opt-in Graphiti knowledge-graph memory backend
 (local stays default)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a memory backend router seam so `forge remember`/`forge recall` can route
to an opt-in Graphiti temporal knowledge-graph tier without changing the clean,
offline local default.

- lib/memory/router.js: single dispatch for remember/recall. Public backends are
  `local | graphiti` only (kernel stays internal). Default `local` is byte-for-byte
  unchanged. Under `graphiti`, writes hit the local JSONL floor first, then fire a
  best-effort, fire-and-forget emit that never throws or blocks — a down sidecar can
  never strand a note. assertMemoryConfigValid gives clear errors when graphiti is
  selected but unconfigured.
- lib/memory/graphiti-mcp.js: DATA-ONLY, locked descriptor
  { name, transport, command, args, envRefs } for the graphiti-memory MCP server.
  envRefs values are ${VAR} references only (no secrets). No file writes — a
  per-harness MCP renderer consumes it in a fast-follow.
- remember/recall route through the router (local behavior identical).
- forge doctor: read-only, non-fatal memory-backend report (does not gate the report).
- skills/memory/SKILL.md (+ .codex mirror): teaches when to remember vs comment and
  how graph memory works (episodes -> entities -> temporal facts).
- docs/guides/memory-backends.md: local default + how to opt into Graphiti (graph DB,
  LLM, privacy/cost). docs/work/2026-07-06-graphiti-memory/research.md: design rationale.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
